        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: сбережения",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сбережения (sberezhéniya) — \"savings\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Все сбережения он потратил на учёбу. Vse sberezhéniya on potrátil na uchyóbu. He spent all his savings on his studies."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural. From сберегать, to save; беречь has the same root."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сбережения (sberezhéniya) is built on сберечь \"to save, to keep\", from беречь \"to protect\", inherited from Proto-Slavic berťi (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
